(1) I'd just been told (MINOR SPOILER FOLLOWS)...that applying a mirror
to a nymph was a good idea.
(2) So the next one I encounter, I apply my mirror in her direction.
(3) "The mountain nymph decides her reflection is beautiful.  She takes
the mirror!" (or that was the gist of the message).
(4) I wander off, find a green-elf, and start beating on the pointy-eared SOB.
(5) "Your mirror breaks.  That's bad luck!"  (huh?  What mirror?).
(6) "Contact jch@cam.cl [ie me!] who may be able to rebuild the game"
(7) "ERROR: freeinv"
(8) When I'm offered a look at my possessions, most of them have vanished.
(9) The game exits cleanly, and I'm recorded in the hiscore table as
having been killed by a panic.

I *think* I may have had two mirrors at the time; could this have been
the problem if they were combined into a single inventory entry?

So, I'm left with a 1195Biggle.e.Z error save file of Biggles the
Barbarian, and (luckily) a cheating save from a few levels back (hey,
there have to be some advantages to being the game administator!). 
Could one of the development team tell me where to take things from
here?  Do you want the error save file, or could you provide pointers as
to which bits of the code to look at?  Should I run around in wizard
mode trying to recreate the error?

